# Delivery control for the backend image (source digest v2 hashes exactly what
# this file lets through). Docker matches patterns from the build-context root,
# so a bare pattern such as `__pycache__` only excludes the ROOT entry; nested
# caches and secrets need the recursive `**/` form. Verified empirically with a
# scratch `FROM scratch` build (see SECURITY_ENGINEERING_RULES SEC-28).

# Environments and secrets (any depth)
**/.env
**/.venv
**/credentials
**/private_keys
**/*.pem
**/*.key

# Virtualenv directories by conventional name (root only: nested `env`/`venv`
# directories may be legitimate source packages)
venv/
env/

# Python caches and compiled files (any depth)
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*$py.class
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache

# Coverage and test artifacts (any depth)
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov
**/coverage.xml

# Local databases (any depth)
**/*.sqlite
**/*.db
**/*.sqlite3

# IDE and temporary files (any depth)
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/*.swp
**/*.swo
**/*~
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# Docker local overrides
docker-compose.override.yml
